WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.187 --> 00:00:01.187
Off we go.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.030
Narrator: This year's Oscars won't include

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.400
a Popular Film category, like
the Academy once proposed.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.800
But, many of your favorites
will still be there.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.570
Campaigning for an Oscar
takes a lot of work

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.010
but nothing like the work that went

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.000
into actually making the movie.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.140
From groundbreaking visual effects

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.290
to daring stunts, to layers of makeup

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.220
there's a lot to admire from
this year's Oscar nominees.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.410
Here's what 2019 Oscar nominees

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:30.963
looked like behind the scenes.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.900
Few movies in the last decade
have altered our culture

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.070
as much as Black Panther did in 2018.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.640
Its showing at the Oscars proves

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.120
that it took blockbuster
filmmaking to new heights.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.720
The movie involves a lot
of demanding stunt work

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.610
from the cast for each
intense fight scene.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.520
Yes, Danai Gurira really did use a wig

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.134
as a defense mechanism.
And yes, Chadwick Boseman

00:01:06.134 --> 00:01:10.990
did kick a guy across a field,
with the help of a few wires.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:14.240
Meanwhile, Michael B.
Jordan went to set every day

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.810
and was covered in around
3,000 prosthetic dots.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.760
Makeup artist Joel Harlow told us

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.620
the fake scars were made to withstand

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.750
the actor's more physical scenes

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.713
as well as the ones where he got wet.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:27.970
And a studio in Atlanta

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.150
was convincingly transformed into Wakanda.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:34.510
That space came complete
with bustling city streets

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.343
and a waterfall that would
become Warrior Falls.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:55.220
Horror movies are often
overlooked during awards season

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:57.560
but this box office and critical success

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.173
was too impressive for
the Oscars to ignore.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.410
While the movie produced
scares from its lack of sound

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:07.500
the ways it did use sound were impressive.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.610
The film's sound team used a strange array

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:11.513
of objects to make Foley sounds.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.090
Crab legs perfectly captured the sound

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:17.870
of the monsters walking.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.740
A combination of celery
and romaine lettuce

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.510
would make the sound of an ear opening.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.453
To figure out the monsters' spine-chilling

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:29.942
echolocation sounds, the
team did some experimenting

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.170
and discovered the best way to do it

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.720
was by tasering a patch of grapes

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.443
and then slowing the sound down.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:56.103
There'll always be a place for
period pieces at the Oscars.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.540
The historical epic, centering
around Mary Queen of Scots

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.720
and Queen Elizabeth I,
and starring Margot Robbie

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.981
and Saoirse Ronan, is
notable for its costumes

00:03:06.981 --> 00:03:10.403
makeup, hairpieces, and sets.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:14.080
The movie was shot on location

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.380
around the United Kingdom and Scotland.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.823
The stars acted with a
literal army of extras.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.690
The Favourite plays a
bit more fast and loose

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:38.600
with history, but it
still flawlessly immerses

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.853
the audience in 18th-century
British aristocratic life.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:45.913
The costumes and wigs are
eye-popping and elaborate.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.560
The movie was shot at
Hatfield House in England.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.720
They stripped many of the
beautiful rooms in the palace

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:57.453
and built a massive bath,
as well as Abigail's room.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.910
The reception of First
Man, which chronicles

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:17.260
Neil Armstrong's trip
to the moon, was mixed.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:19.010
But one thing nobody can deny

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:20.873
is that it's visually stunning.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:26.460
Its set pieces are as
historically accurate as possible.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.690
Production designer Nathan Crowley told us

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:31.350
that the lunar module and space capsule

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.930
were built to scale.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.010
Meanwhile, the Saturn V
model seen in the movie

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.830
was actually just 14 feet tall.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:42.990
That's about 1/25th the
size of the actual rocket.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.320
Some of the models could even move.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:49.280
In some scenes, to convincingly
replicate zero gravity

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.930
they put the camera below the actors.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:55.283
A technique that has been used
in many movies set in space.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.750
The moon landing sequence,
which is shot in IMAX

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.090
will actually make you feel
like you're walking on the moon.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:08.060
Some parts of this sequence
were shot in a quarry.

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:09.310
Other parts were shot on

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.773
a very convincing-looking soundstage.

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:15.410
The stunts were equally impressive.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.280
Gosling allowed himself to be launched

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:21.010
out of a capsule, and
then got dragged around

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:22.933
in the movie's most daring stunt.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.220
What sets A Star is Born apart is that

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.560
all the concert scenes were filmed live

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:49.740
and Bradley Cooper and Lady Gaga

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.130
are always performing together.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:54.740
Even for two people as talented as them

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.833
they still had to rehearse a lot.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.430
A big part of the
production was sound editing

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:03.630
which required layering multiple sounds

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.130
in a single scene, including the vocals.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:07.953
All of which were sung live.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.740
Wes Anderson's second
stop-motion animated feature

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:29.130
was one of the best
animated movies of 2018.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.670
It's staggering just to look at

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:32.610
the numbers behind the movie.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.550
Isle of Dogs animators were working with

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:39.020
around 1,105 puppets on set.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.080
A single sushi making
sequence from the movie

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.673
took six to eight months to bring to life.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.270
Animators, meanwhile, had to
use pins and wooden sticks

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.640
to move the dogs' eyeballs and lips around

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.360
to make the characters move realistically.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:56.920
The animators even painstakingly
moved the fur around

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.690
to give the impression that dog's fur

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:00.960
was blowing in the wind.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:04.220
Stop-motion animation requires
faces to get changed out

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.870
for each different mood and emotion.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:10.310
Andy Gent, the head of the
movie's puppet department

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.720
told us that the character's
fur made this process

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.463
much more difficult than usual.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.980
Marvel's most ambitious movie yet

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:34.150
didn't quite get the same
awards love as Black Panther

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:36.730
but it still managed
to make an appearance.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:38.830
The biggest standout technical aspect

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:41.410
of the latest Avengers was Josh Brolin's

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:44.300
towering performance as Thanos.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.130
The actor performed in
a motion capture suit

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:50.600
for a character who would
then be created using CGI.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:53.820
Because Thanos is so
tall, Brolin often acted

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.140
with an object on top of his head.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.400
That way, actors would know where exactly

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.550
they should be looking.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.700
Motion-capture technology
has gotten so good

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.140
that Thanos felt real.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:08.930
Honestly, it's about time
the Academy starts taking

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.080
motion-capture performances
more seriously.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.550
The long-awaited sequel involved

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:32.400
a cast of very committed actors.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.820
Meanwhile, production designers created

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:39.263
a very accurate version of
1930s London inside a studio.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:44.830
For this shot, in which Mary
Poppins falls into a bathtub

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.810
they built a giant slide beneath the tub

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:49.593
that Emily Blunt had to
slide down backwards.

